  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract activity in California for FY2026 to date totals $40.7B in obligations across 180,294 awards, with an average award size of $226K. Obligations fell 34.4% year over year from the prior fiscal period. Annual historical figures show obligations of $52.1B in FY21, $57.5B in FY22, $61.5B in FY23, $61.7B in FY24, and $62B in FY25, before the current-year total of $40.7B. That makes the FY2026 to date total materially smaller than the most recent full fiscal year totals. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer in the state at $21.4B, followed by the Department of Energy at $6B and the Department of Homeland Security at $4.7B. Spending is concentrated in research and development, construction, shipbuilding, and aircraft-related industries, with the single largest NAICS category at $5.5B. On the vendor side, federal obligations are concentrated: LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC received $3.3B, FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO received $2.5B, and NATIONAL STEEL AND SHIPBUILDING COMPANY received $1.9B.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What explains the year-over-year drop in obligations?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 34.4% year over year to $40.7B, a clear decline versus recent full-year totals. FY25 obligations were $62B, so the FY2026 to date total is substantially lower than that prior annual level. Part of the shift reflects reduced buying by large federal customers compared with the prior fiscal year mix. The drop also shows up across high-dollar sectors that dominated earlier years, including research and development and construction."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate federal buying in California?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer at $21.4B, followed by the Department of Energy at $6B and the Department of Homeland Security at $4.7B. On the vendor side, LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC leads with $3.3B, then FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO with $2.5B and NATIONAL STEEL AND SHIPBUILDING COMPANY with $1.9B. Top industries by obligations include research and development at $5.5B and related R&D at $4.9B, plus Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $3.8B."
      }
    ]
  },
